{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1380861-werewolf-the-apocalypse-homebrew-5th-edition","id":1380861,"title":"Werewolf the Apocalypse Homebrew 5th Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-12T21:41:46-07:00","id":1380861,"title":"Werewolf the Apocalypse Homebrew 5th Edition","content":"This is just my take on what the system could look like. I made this in a stream of boredom and out of slight necessity for werewolves in my V5 campaign where I'm telling a story of Chicago by Night at multiple tables and wanted to capture the POV of the werewolves in Chicago as well as the vamps. Hope everyone likes. I intend to continue to work onto it until I can perfect the neccessary changes like merits and gifts. I'm looking forward fo comments and creative thoughts that can potentially help me improve the system until W5 actually comes out.<br /> <br /> Character Sheet: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1FmZtP6Jfpqe5Ttpp26iW62QLGveIcmTP\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/open?id=1Fm...iW62QLGveIcmTP</a><br /> <br /> <br /> Base Rules: <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1GvamiZGNkYus7PIAGKxf-XoVrqEpOghP/view?usp=drivesdk\" target=\"_blank\">https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Gva...w?usp=drivesdk</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26094,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26094-thatoneguy","user":"ThatOneGuy","date":".  Adjusted Moon Signs as well as included a Character sheet for anyone who wants to throw werewolves into their table. 04-14-2020, 01:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26094-thatoneguy","name":"ThatOneGuy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T06:46:04-07:00","id":1380932,"title":"","content":"Nice! thanks for sharing. Many things I liked in here. Primal-urge as BP equivalent has been talked about a lot on Hunters forum so I do like that. Also like the idea of rage threshold. You should ask if you can post this over in the Hunter's discord. Could spark discussions form those their.<br /> <br /> Couple of things I would Change for my personal game though would be:<br /> <br /> It seems harder to get rid of rage once it builds. Seems mostly you have to go pick a fight or the moon has to be right and I like to add a bit of agency to this so I think I would also sooth a rage anytime they gain Gnosis. I would also switch the levels for the amount of rage you sooth for each of the moon phases meaning you aren't calmer when it is a full moon out you are less calm. <br /> <br /> Other than that, I would remove the Starting Gnosis and cap both Rage and Gnosis at 5 I think that would be all I would do to use this in games.<br /> <br /> I think that is it for my personal game. really appreciate you sharing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T08:07:33-07:00","id":1380951,"title":"","content":"Thanks for the feedback. Glad you liked it. I definitely like the idea about switching the moon signs. That makes perfect sense actually. As far as rage going to 7 I did that because rage is the deciding factor of your frenzy difficulty. And all 5th ed difficulties raise to 7. Also with vampires hunger caps at 5 because they just frenzy. Garou have a more dangerous stage beyond frenzy. Thrall of the worm is the danger of rage increasing too far which is rage 6+. As far Gnosis goes, I like your additive of dropping rage when replenishing Gnosis, but I struggled alot figuring out how to balance Gnosis to make the choice of breed still be important and relevant to character creation. I would like to post this on hunters discord, how would I go about getting on there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26094-thatoneguy","name":"ThatOneGuy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T11:40:29-07:00","id":1381040,"title":"","content":"To me the choice of breed/tribe/auspice should be 1 part the story you wish to tell and the second part is a small mechanical benefit that is balanced but not so overpowered that it outweighs other choices. Like gift selection or a Homid's silver benefit. Since you were looking at forsaken for some inspiration maybe use gift trees and figure out incitement though gift access. Just a thought. I really like what you have done so far though.<br /> <br /> Yes the 7 cap makes sense with that logic. Just to note though Vampires don't just frenzy they still have to be provoked and then that provocation sets the difficulty for their willpower roll to see if they resist. for example having hunger 4 opens both seeing/smelling blood (difficulty 2) and Tasting blood (Difficulty 3).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-13T12:18:07-07:00","id":1381059,"title":"","content":"Thanks very much Refwulfe! Glad the majority of representation fit both mechanics and roleplay. I have definitely been looking to forsaken to adopt their gift trees, however for the last couple games I've allowed gifts from either game, until balancing can be determined for what does and doesnt work. I made the moon phase change immediately btw, it's perfect for the role the moon plays for garou. Thanks again for your comments and thoughts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26094-thatoneguy","name":"ThatOneGuy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}